# Pulse tick: `/desk` — the explore lab's ALLOCATOR. A weekly whole-corpus pass
# that writes a <=1,200-word chief-of-research resourcing memo to
# ~/explore/refs/desk/<date>.md, files `desk:` beads, and push-notifies the top
# ask + the PATH. It never touches Asana. Successor to pulse-elevate.service
# (rename 2026-07-26, explore-mqvu).
#
# The memo is a DESTINATION Zig walks into after the tick has ended (explore-b47q),
# so the artifact on disk — not the tick's transcript — is the deliverable.
#
# tmux WINDOW: `desk` since 2026-07-27. Zig's call on explore-lsnr is ONE DURABLE
# WINDOW PER LOOP — each loop with its own ledger row and its own offboard/handoff.
# This unit previously injected into `elevate`, which it SHARED with Zig's manual
# /elevate working session; that window is now his alone and he expects to retire
# it when his current work there is done.
#
# What moved with the flip (2026-07-27):
#   - `--window elevate` -> `--window desk` (this file; machine-local, uncommitted)
#   - identity key `desk:` added to ~/explore/.claude/identity.yml (grants: [llm])
#   - refs/session-handoff--desk.md SEEDED from refs/session-handoff--elevate.md.
#     Seeded, not moved: the elevate note stays with Zig's live session. The desk
#     window is created fresh by pulse-inject on the next fire, so without the seed
#     the tick would onboard from the (nonexistent) legacy refs/session-handoff.md.
# What did NOT move: the ledger row is still `desk` (rows key on the `row` field,
#   never on the window), so no ledger seed is needed and none was written. The
#   timer, its schedule, and the carried-across stamp are untouched.
#
# Inspect runs: journalctl --user -u pulse-desk.service -n 20
[Unit]
Description=Pulse tick: weekly /desk pass (explore lab resourcing memo)

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=%h/.agents/agents/scheduler/pulse-inject.sh --loop %p --dir /home/ubuntu/explore --session zig-computer --window desk --cmd "/desk /home/ubuntu/explore" --launch "claude --permission-mode bypassPermissions"
